---
import NoteFigure from './NoteFigure.astro';
const indices = [0, 1, 2, 3];
const subscripts = ['₁', '₂', '₃', '₄'];
---

<NoteFigure
  label="Autoregressive structure"
  title="A simple determinant can still hide a sequential inverse"
  caption="The four-coordinate Jacobian redraws page 36's lower-triangular dependency pattern. Positive diagonal scales, MAF/IAF direction comparisons and network-pass arrows are editorial expansions. MAF parameters depend on earlier data coordinates; IAF parameters depend on earlier noise coordinates. IAF can evaluate its own generated sample's density using its known noise and volume corrections, while a new external observation requires a sequential inverse."
>
  <div class="autoregressive-panels">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 490" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-autoregressive-matrix-title flow-autoregressive-matrix-desc">
      <title id="flow-autoregressive-matrix-title">Autoregressive layer Jacobian with zero upper triangle and nonzero diagonal</title>
      <desc id="flow-autoregressive-matrix-desc">In a four-coordinate layer, output v i depends only on input coordinates u one through u i. The matrix has zeros above the diagonal, arbitrary entries below, and positive exp alpha i diagonal entries. The log absolute determinant is the sum of alpha i. Triangularity must be accompanied by invertible coordinate transformations.</desc>
      <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Earlier coordinates only</text>
      {indices.map((j) => (
        <text x={115 + j * 50} y="67" text-anchor="middle" class="coordinate">u{subscripts[j]}</text>
      ))}
      {indices.map((i) => (
        <text x="57" y={114 + i * 50} text-anchor="middle" class="coordinate">v{subscripts[i]}</text>
      ))}
      <path d="M 92 82 H 83 V 286 H 92 M 292 82 H 301 V 286 H 292" class="bracket" />
      {indices.map((i) => indices.map((j) => (
        <g>
          <rect x={95 + j * 50} y={91 + i * 50} width="40" height="40" rx="3" class={i === j ? 'diagonal' : 'cell'} />
          {i === j ? (
            <text x={115 + j * 50} y={115 + i * 50} text-anchor="middle" class="diagonal-label">e<tspan baseline-shift="super" class="exponent">α{subscripts[i]}</tspan></text>
          ) : (
            <text x={115 + j * 50} y={117 + i * 50} text-anchor="middle" class={j > i ? 'zero' : 'free'}>{j > i ? '0' : '∗'}</text>
          )}
        </g>
      )))}
      <text x="170" y="322" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">Diagonal: exp(αᵢ) ≠ 0</text>
      <text x="170" y="351" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Later inputs have zero influence.</text>
      <text x="170" y="387" text-anchor="middle" class="formula">log |det J| = Σᵢ αᵢ</text>
      <path d="M 16 409 H 324" class="divider" />
      <text x="170" y="441" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Triangular alone is not enough:</text>
      <text x="170" y="466" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">each coordinate map must be invertible.</text>
    </svg>

    <svg viewBox="0 0 340 490" role="img" aria-labelledby="flow-autoregressive-directions-title flow-autoregressive-directions-desc">
      <title id="flow-autoregressive-directions-title">MAF has parallel density evaluation while IAF has parallel generation</title>
      <desc id="flow-autoregressive-directions-desc">MAF maps an observed data vector x through a masked network whose parameters use earlier x coordinates, obtaining all noise coordinates z in parallel. Its sampling direction is sequential. IAF maps known noise z through a masked network whose parameters use earlier z coordinates, obtaining all data coordinates x in parallel. Its inverse for an arbitrary observed x is sequential. Stacked flow layers remain sequential in both models.</desc>
      <defs>
        <marker id="flow-autoregressive-direction-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="8" refY="5" markerWidth="5" markerHeight="5" orient="auto"><path d="M 1 1 L 8 5 L 1 9" class="arrowhead" /></marker>
      </defs>
      <text x="170" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="panel-title">Which direction is parallel?</text>
      <text x="170" y="62" text-anchor="middle" class="family">MAF: density direction</text>
      <g class="node">
        <rect x="17" y="86" width="60" height="57" rx="4" />
        <rect x="112" y="86" width="116" height="57" rx="4" />
        <rect x="263" y="86" width="60" height="57" rx="4" />
      </g>
      <text x="47" y="121" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">x</text>
      <text x="170" y="108" text-anchor="middle" class="small">μ, α from</text>
      <text x="170" y="131" text-anchor="middle" class="small">earlier x</text>
      <text x="293" y="121" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">z</text>
      <g class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-autoregressive-direction-arrow)"><path d="M 83 114 H 106" /><path d="M 234 114 H 257" /></g>
      <text x="170" y="171" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">Density: all of x is already known.</text>
      <text x="170" y="197" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Sampling: generate x₁ → x₂ → …</text>
      <path d="M 16 218 H 324" class="divider" />
      <text x="170" y="249" text-anchor="middle" class="family">IAF: generation direction</text>
      <g class="node">
        <rect x="17" y="273" width="60" height="57" rx="4" />
        <rect x="112" y="273" width="116" height="57" rx="4" />
        <rect x="263" y="273" width="60" height="57" rx="4" />
      </g>
      <text x="47" y="308" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">z</text>
      <text x="170" y="295" text-anchor="middle" class="small">μ, α from</text>
      <text x="170" y="318" text-anchor="middle" class="small">earlier z</text>
      <text x="293" y="308" text-anchor="middle" class="symbol">x</text>
      <g class="forward" marker-end="url(#flow-autoregressive-direction-arrow)"><path d="M 83 301 H 106" /><path d="M 234 301 H 257" /></g>
      <text x="170" y="359" text-anchor="middle" class="accent">Sampling: all of z is already known.</text>
      <text x="170" y="385" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">External x: recover z₁ → z₂ → …</text>
      <path d="M 16 408 H 324" class="divider" />
      <text x="170" y="438" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">IAF own-sample density is also cheap.</text>
      <text x="170" y="466" text-anchor="middle" class="muted">Layer stacking is sequential for both.</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
</NoteFigure>

<style>
  .autoregressive-panels { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
  svg { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 400px; margin-inline: auto; }
  text { fill: var(--ink); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; }
  .panel-title { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .coordinate { font-size: 18px; }
  .symbol { font-size: 23px; font-style: italic; }
  .family { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; }
  .formula { font-size: 18px; }
  .small, .muted { font-size: 13px; }
  .muted, .zero { fill: var(--muted); }
  .accent, .diagonal-label { fill: var(--accent); }
  .diagonal-label { font-size: 20px; }
  .exponent { font-size: 10px; }
  .free { font-size: 22px; }
  .cell { fill: none; stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 0.8; }
  .diagonal { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--accent); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .node { fill: var(--paper); stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .bracket { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .forward, .arrowhead { fill: none; stroke: var(--ink); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .divider { stroke: var(--line); stroke-width: 1; }
  @container (max-width: 580px) { .autoregressive-panels { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2rem; } }
</style>
